handoff:
defer: a project wanting a different default, or a lease long enough to wedge a ticket

Leases stop a remote claim from wedging a ticket, but nothing can confirm a
remote agent is alive right now — that would need a shared medium updating
in real time, which is a server, and is out of scope permanently. What is
open is only whether the durations want to be a project's choice rather than
each caller's.

Today PIDLY_LEASE is per-invocation and there is no default: an agent
without a local process must name a duration every time. A project where
every cloud agent should hold for two hours has no way to say so, and a
project where nothing should hold longer than fifteen minutes has no way to
enforce it.

The obstacle is that pidly has no configuration file. schema.md is the only
file a project owns, and it describes tickets, not the tool. Adding a config
file is a larger decision than the setting that would go in it — and 28 is
about to make the schema file a stanza format that could hold a stanza that
is not a field, which is either the natural home or the beginning of a
mess.

Trigger: a project actually wanting a different default, or a lease long
enough to wedge a ticket in practice.
